{
  "_README": [
    "Shrink-only baseline for hardcoded NSW zone-code literals.",
    "",
    "WHY A BASELINE AND NOT A HARD ZERO: the tree-wide sweep finds 270 across",
    "~90 files. Failing on all of them would block every merge on day one and",
    "the guard would be deleted within a week. So: this number may go DOWN and",
    "never UP, per file. Same shape as scripts/check_test_baselines.py.",
    "",
    "WHY IT WAS NEEDED: lint_hardcoded_zone_codes.py already had an --all mode",
    "and already covered .ts/.tsx, but it was only ever run diff-scoped from",
    "pre-commit. So every violation that already existed was invisible",
    "permanently -- a rule that only applies to future code cleans nothing up.",
    "That is how issue #928 (a live zone->permitted-use table serving the UI)",
    "and lib/setbacks/validator.ts (minimum lot size by zone) both survived.",
    "",
    "TO LOWER A NUMBER: fix the file, re-run",
    "  python scripts/lint_hardcoded_zone_codes.py --baseline --update",
    "and commit. Lowering is the point; the ratchet exists to stop it rising."
  ],
